codemap 9
tour tour-tree
kind data
author ai
group map
note A tour is a tree, stored flat. Every step carries the id of the step it hangs under (None for a root) and nothing else; the tree shape is derived on demand, in pre-order, roots in list order and children in list order. That is what makes a flow readable top-down, and it is also why editing is cheap: appending a step is a push, deleting one moves its children up to its parent, and re-parenting is a single field plus a cycle check. Inside the model a step is named by its StepId, which never changes. The CLI's step indices are positions in the step list, turned into ids at the command line and never stored.

